# GitHub reads this file to show a "Cite this repository" button.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its benchmark results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Byte-Sized Brain"
version: 0.2.0
abstract: >-
  A reproducible benchmark of post-training quantization. It trains a feed-forward
  network on MNIST, a MobileNetV2 CNN on CIFAR-10, an LSTM on IMDB and DistilBERT on
  IMDB, converts each to TFLite or ONNX Runtime with INT8 or dynamic-range
  quantization, and measures model size, accuracy, latency and memory with one shared
  harness. Committed results are from an x86-64 CPU, and the same code runs on ARM64.
authors:
  - given-names: Vardh
    family-names: Jain
repository-code: "https://github.com/vardhjain/Byte-Sized-Brain"
url: "https://vardhjain.github.io/Byte-Sized-Brain/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - quantization
  - post-training quantization
  - model compression
  - edge machine learning
  - TensorFlow Lite
  - ONNX Runtime
  - benchmarking
